&lt;p&gt;This is a very exciting opportunity to join Verkada’s growing legal team as its first and lead Global Corporate Counsel. You will report directly to the General Counsel and work hand–in-hand with Verkada’s executive leadership as a trusted legal advisor on a wide variety of corporate legal issues across the company. Your first priority will be to guide us through IPO readiness, and then lead the company’s legal strategy behind its capital structures, public company reporting obligations, corporate governance, complex transactions, board management, and regulatory compliance. From day one, you will need to roll up your sleeves and do the work, as you will operate on a lean team of “one” while you lay the foundation necessary to scale our global corporate legal function and eventually build a rockstar team. If you enjoy building from the ground up, this role is for you!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to a thriving in-office culture, so we expect this role to be onsite in our office in San Mateo, CA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll&amp;nbsp; Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the legal roadmap for IPO and public company readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish compliance frameworks, draft and manage future SEC reporting structures , and implement rigorous internal governance policies, including insider trading protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct all corporate governance initiatives for Verkada and its international subsidiaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the preparation of materials, agendas, resolutions, and stockholder compliance structures for our Board of Directors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead legal strategy and execution for all strategic corporate transactions while managing outside counsel to ensure seamless due diligence and post-acquisition integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the structuring and execution of complex corporate finance initiatives, including debt facilities, syndicated credit lines, private funding rounds, and capital allocation frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Verkada’s Finance, Stock Administration, and People teams to oversee equity compensation programs, capitalization table management, and secondary market transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor new and emerging developments in applicable worldwide regulations and laws that could impact Verkada’s corporate governance and structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
