&lt;li&gt;Undergraduate degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or similar quantitative field. MS, PhD, or MBA optional&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven history of launching and scaling hardware and/or embedded systems products. Strong customer intuition, technical depth, and ability to navigate tradeoffs are critical to success in this role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited to roll up your sleeves and get out of the office. You&#39;ll spend time with installers, integrators, and customers deploying in unwired environments. You&#39;ll use that insight to shape the product!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to build platform and recurring-revenue business models. You bring a structured mindset to ambiguous problems, from data plan pricing and carrier economics to attach-rate modeling and ROI analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead across strategy and execution. We pride ourselves in sweating the details and search for this in candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real passion for craftsmanship and product details. If you&#39;ve spent days retrofitting your house with the latest smart home technology, you&#39;ll like it here&lt;/li&gt;
