&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verkada is transforming how organizations protect their people and places with an integrated, privacy-sensitive AI-powered platform that includes solutions for video security, access control, air quality sensors, alarms, intercoms, and visitor management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve got serious momentum in the market: more than 30,000 customers (including 100+ of the Fortune 500), &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cnbc.com/2025/12/03/verkada-capitalg-valuation-security.html&quot;&gt;a $5.8B valuation&lt;/a&gt;, more than $1 billion in annualized bookings, and backing from CapitalG, Sequoia Capital, General Catalyst, Felicis Ventures, Next47 and more. Physical AI is one of the most consequential technology shifts of our time, and Verkada is at the center of it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can look at all kinds of communities to see our platform’s impact in the world. It&#39;s the retailer that uses our agentic AI to deter theft before it happens. The warehouse that uses AI-powered alerts to make sure its team is protected on the floor with proper PPE. The school that’s alerted to a threat in real-time and triggers a lockdown in seconds, not minutes. We’re rapidly scaling this impact: today, more than 2 million Verkada devices are deployed across 170+ countries.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Alarms team builds systems that detect, verify, and respond to real-world security threats using sensors, cameras, and AI. You’ll work on products that are critical during high-stakes moments and directly impact customer safety.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate as a small, fast-moving team with significant ownership, collaborating across mobile, backend, and firmware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Android Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to help build and maintain the mobile experience for our Alarms product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is focused on developing high-quality mobile applications used for real-time monitoring, alerts, and incident response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also work on device-facing experiences, including building &lt;strong&gt;native Linux-based UIs&lt;/strong&gt; for embedded products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain features across&lt;strong&gt; Android And iOS mobile applications&lt;/strong&gt; for the Alarms product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop real-time user experiences for alerts, video, and system status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with product, design, backend, and firmware teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, maintainable, and performant code across mobile platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape architecture and technical direction for mobile development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to &lt;strong&gt;embedded / Linux UI development&lt;/strong&gt; for hardware products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of software Android development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of mobile UI/UX patterns and performance considerations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with APIs and asynchronous systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product mindset with attention to usability and reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
