&lt;li&gt;Lead programming, test fits, space planning, and floor plan development for new offices, labs, and workplace renovations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce and maintain complete architectural drawing sets, construction documents, and custom interior and millwork details using AutoCAD, Revit, or similar drafting software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain Verkada&#39;s workplace design standards, CAD template libraries, and CAFM infrastructure to support a growing real estate portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale the Workplace Design function, including hiring, mentoring, and developing future Space and Occupancy Planning team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary architectural coordinator across Mechanical, Electrical, Plumbing (MEP), IT, AV, low-voltage, and physical security disciplines to ensure seamless integration within workplace projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct constructability reviews during design development to proactively identify conflicts and improve project execution before construction begins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Designers, Project Managers, consultants, and general contractors throughout design and construction to maintain quality, schedule, and design intent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with business leaders to align workplace layouts with headcount forecasts, operational requirements, and future growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop efficient, scalable workplace planning strategies that maximize employee experience while supporting evolving business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all workplace designs comply with applicable building codes, accessibility requirements, and Verkada&#39;s internal design standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
