&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Architecture, Interior Architecture, or a related technical design field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–8+ years of experience in commercial architecture, workplace design, or corporate interiors, with experience leading projects from concept through construction administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert proficiency in AutoCAD, Revit, or comparable architectural drafting software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of commercial building systems, including MEP coordination, construction detailing, ADA requirements, and applicable building codes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience producing comprehensive construction documentation and coordinating multidisciplinary consultant teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership experience managing projects, mentoring team members, or leading complex cross-functional initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong spatial planning skills with exceptional attention to detail and a passion for creating high-performing workplace environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency with Google Workspace, particularly Google Sheets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CAFM platforms, preferably OfficeSpace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational, communication, and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple concurrent projects in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting workplace growth within a technology company or other high-growth organization is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
