&lt;p&gt;We are actively looking for an experienced front-end engineer to join our core engineering group, with a specific focus on our Design Systems and UI architecture. As a crucial driver of our user interface, you will build, scale, and maintain the foundational component library that powers our enterprise applications. You will act as the vital bridge between Design and Engineering, partnering closely with&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;8+ product teams&lt;/strong&gt; to deliver a cohesive, accessible, and beautiful web experience that supports a suite of connected devices at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will go beyond building individual features; you will help evolve the UI architecture and design tokens that ensure consistency and accelerate development. While your primary focus will be on the Platform UI and Design System, you will operate within a highly collaborative platform environment with opportunities to engage with our broader microfrontend and core infrastructure initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evolve the Design System:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with engineering leadership to develop and scale our centralized, React-based component library, ensuring it remains highly reusable and easy to consume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bridge Design and Engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner deeply with the Product Design team to translate design visions and Figma tokens into robust, pixel-perfect, and interactive web components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empower product engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; Support, collaborate with, and mentor engineers across 8+ distinct product teams, driving system adoption and helping them implement UI best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion Accessibility (a11y):&lt;/strong&gt; Advocate for and implement strict accessibility standards (WCAG) across all shared components, ensuring our enterprise products are inclusive and usable by everyone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ensure UI Quality and Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Write comprehensive automated tests (unit, visual regression) for components, and optimize UI rendering performance for complex single-page applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Documentation and Tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain excellent documentation (e.g., via Storybook) and usage guidelines, making it frictionless for product teams to discover and implement components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to the Broader Platform:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure the design system integrates seamlessly into our massive microfrontend architecture, with opportunities to contribute to core frontend tooling and infrastructure as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
